[h1]R.A.T.S. Pop-Out Windows[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]
[b]Bugs, ideas, questions:[/b] [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/popout]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]

[b]Your windows, your way.[/b]
Windows that stay where you put them, snap, maximize and go see-through. Throw them onto a second monitor with one click, and use an Encyclopedia you can actually search. All of it works on one monitor too.

[h2]The highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Second monitor in one click.[/b] A pop-out entry in every window's menu moves the window over, the same entry brings it back. Your desktop stays visible around the windows
[*][b]Windows that remember.[/b] Position and size are kept, also after a restart, and popped-out windows come back where you left them
[*][b]Snap, maximize, see-through.[/b] Windows snap to each other and the screen edges, double-click the title bar to maximize, opacity and scale per window
[*][b]An Encyclopedia that finds things.[/b] Search finds unit ids and description words: "Type 072" finds the Yukan class
[/list]

[h2]Second monitor[/h2]
[list]
[*]One menu button in the title bar of the formation manager, message log, unit status, camera, sensor and doctrine windows
[*]Over there only the windows show; they can be bigger than the game normally allows
[*]Connect the monitor before starting the game
[/list]

[h2]All windows[/h2]
[list]
[*]Wide resize corners and proper resize cursors
[*]Window look in the same menu: opacity, scale, text outline, and whether a window stays below or above the others
[*]Settings in the same menu, in the game's nine languages
[*]Optional desktops: Tab switches between window layouts (off by default)
[/list]

[h2]Encyclopedia[/h2]
[list]
[*]Loadout variants get real names ("Long-Hull [Early]") instead of bare years, sorted by service date
[*]A click on a class opens its earliest variant; "Armed only"; the country list only offers countries with units for your search
[*]Drag the edge of the unit list to widen or hide it
[*]Weapon and sensor links show their description as a tooltip
[*]Your country, category and search stay set for next time
[/list]

[h2]In a mission and in campaigns[/h2]
[list]
[*]Unit Status: full unit name, a Reference tab with the unit's data and loadouts, taller damage control sections
[*]Right-click the flag or name in the unit panel for the unit's menu (also for contacts)
[*]The time panel can be dragged anywhere. Clicking a message in the corner log jumps to its unit
[*]Task Force Builder: loadouts oldest first, a "Strict loadouts" option on the start screen
[*]Damaged ships can be dismissed, and the hull-swap price is fixed
[/list]
Every part has its own switch, so turn off whatever you don't want.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
The window handling is based on rgreat's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3813683442]Smart Windows[/url] mod.

[h2]Install and game versions[/h2]
[b]R.A.T.S. Keel[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]subscribe[/url] and switch it on in the Mods menu; its page has the one install step. It replaces Anchor Chain.
Windows. A second monitor only for the pop-out part.
Made for Sea Power 0.8.7. On the 3D globe public beta (build 261107) the mod starts and its menu button is there; popping a window out was not run there yet. Works next to the game's own second-monitor map and world view. No game files are changed.

[h2]Settings[/h2]
The menu has a settings panel, or edit [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\[/i]: [i]dev.sewerlabs.seapowerpopout.cfg[/i] (second monitor) and [i]dev.sewerlabs.seapowerpopout.smartwindows.cfg[/i] (everything else).

[h2]Problems, feedback, ideas[/h2]
Post bugs, feedback and ideas on the [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/popout]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]. For a bug, add [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] (as a link).

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerPopOut]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerPopOut[/url]

